{#
insight/_pane.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
The insight strip: a band of up to three cards above the mail list, saying the
thing before the mail that carries it does — a parcel out for delivery, a
flight tomorrow, a pull request waiting on eyes.

Rendered alone, as the whole response of the lazy `app_insight_pane` fragment,
into the frame the mailbox layout leaves for it.

Accepts:
  rows  list<MailInsight>  from InsightPane::rowsFor(), soonest first, already
        capped at InsightPane::MAX_ROWS and already EMPTY for all three of the
        reasons the strip may not exist — switched off, nothing upcoming, waved
        away. This template applies none of those rules and re-checks none of
        them; it renders what it is given.

An empty `rows` renders NOTHING — no heading, no empty state, no bordered box.
That is not politeness, it is the deal InsightPane's class doc strikes with
HappeningSoonController: this band is allowed above the list only because it
costs nothing on the days it has nothing to say, and those are most days for
most people. An "on your radar" box saying it looked and found nothing would
spend attention above the inbox every morning to report an absence.

The frame element itself is still rendered in that case, and has to be: it is
what Turbo swaps the lazy load into, and a response without it is a frame that
never finishes loading. Empty, it has no content and therefore no height.

HEIGHT, not width. The strip is a band above the list rather than a column
beside it, so no pane loses a pixel it had — that is the answer InsightPane
gives to the objection on the record against a fourth region, and it is why
everything below is sized by its content and nothing here grows.

The card vocabulary is _insight_strip's and the radar panel's, deliberately:
the same kind chip, the same status tones, the same one primary action. Three
visual languages for one object would make a parcel look like three different
things depending on where the user met it.

One Stimulus scope over the whole band, so both CSRF tokens are minted once
rather than once per row — the split radar_controller documents, plus the
pane-wide token the ✕ needs.
#}

{% set rows = rows|default([]) %}

<turbo-frame id="insight_pane">
    {% if rows is not empty %}
        <div data-insight-pane
             data-controller="insight--pane"
             data-insight--pane-token-value="{{ csrf_token('insight-dismiss') }}"
             data-insight--pane-pane-token-value="{{ csrf_token('insight-pane-dismiss') }}"
             data-insight--pane-pane-url-value="{{ path('app_insight_pane_dismiss') }}"
             {# Its own card, beside the mail card rather than on it.

                This was a box drawn inside .main-pane for two releases, and
                drawing separation was never going to be enough: a child of the
                mail card reads as that card's header however it is styled. The
                layout now gives the strip and the mail card a column of their
                own (see _layout/_mailbox.html.twig), so the chrome here is the
                chrome of a PANE — the same border, radius and soft surface the
                sidebar and the calendar pane wear, on the app background,
                with the column's gutter doing the separating.

                `pane` and not a hand-assembled lookalike: it is the utility
                the topbar and the sidebar already wear, so the surface, the
                blur, the border, the radius and the two-layer shadow are the
                app's one definition of what a pane looks like rather than a
                second opinion that drifts. The first version reached for
                shadow-pop, which is the MENU shadow — built for something
                floating over the page — and the strip read as a dropdown
                parked above the mail instead of as a pane beside it.

                No `shell-chrome`: that marks furniture, and the flat layout
                strips its card so only the mail pane keeps a box. This is
                content sitting beside that box and keeps its own. #}
             {# The gutter to the mail pane belongs to this element and not
                to the column, so an absent strip leaves no gap behind it. #}
             class="shrink-0 pane px-3 py-2 mb-gutter">

            <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2">
                <p class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-ink-faint">
                    {{ 'insights.pane.heading'|trans }}
                </p>

                <button type="button"
                        data-action="click->insight--pane#dismissPane"
                        data-insight-pane-dismiss
                        aria-label="{{ 'insights.pane.dismiss_all'|trans }}"
                        title="{{ 'insights.pane.dismiss_all'|trans }}"
                        class="-mr-1 flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full
                               text-ink-faint hover:bg-hover hover:text-ink transition-colors">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-xmark text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                </button>
            </div>

            <ul class="mt-1.5 divide-y divide-line" data-insight-list>
                {% for insight in rows %}
                    {% set trackingUrl = insight.payload.trackingUrl|default(null) %}
                    {% set externalUrl = insight.payload.url|default(null) %}
                    {% set status      = insight.payload.status|default(null) %}
                    {# Only the vocabulary the catalogue knows — an extractor's
                       stray status must not print a raw key onto a card. The
                       one place raw colours are spelled out, and the same five
                       lines the radar and the reading-pane strip use. #}
                    {% set statusTone = {
                        'announced':        'border-ink-faint/40 text-ink-muted',
                        'in_transit':       'border-sky-500/40 text-sky-700 dark:text-sky-300',
                        'out_for_delivery': 'border-amber-500/40 text-amber-700 dark:text-amber-300',
                        'delivered':        'border-green-500/40 text-green-700 dark:text-green-300',
                    }[status] ?? null %}

                    <li data-insight-card
                        data-insight-id="{{ insight.id }}"
                        data-insight-kind="{{ insight.kind.value }}"
                        class="flex items-center gap-2.5 py-1.5">

                        {% include 'insight/_kind_chip.html.twig' with { kind: insight.kind, size: 'h-8 w-8' } only %}

                        <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
                            <p class="truncate text-sm font-semibold text-ink" title="{{ insight.title }}">
                                {{ insight.title }}
                            </p>

                            <p class="truncate text-xs text-ink-faint">
                                {% if insight.happensAt is not null %}
                                    {# The near-date ladder the message list already
                                       uses (see _partials/_thread_row.html.twig):
                                       compare whole days as the reader's clock has
                                       them, then hand the wording to `intl_date` so
                                       German gets its own field order rather than an
                                       English pattern with German words in it.

                                       A week is the width of the ladder because that
                                       is how long a weekday name stays unambiguous —
                                       "Thursday" nine days out is a puzzle, not a
                                       date. #}
                                    {% set day     = insight.happensAt|date('Y-m-d') %}
                                    {% set today   = 'now'|date('Y-m-d') %}
                                    {% set nextDay = 'now'|date_modify('+1 day')|date('Y-m-d') %}

                                    {% if day == today %}
                                        {{ 'insights.pane.when.today'|trans }}
                                    {% elseif day == nextDay %}
                                        {{ 'insights.pane.when.tomorrow'|trans }}
                                    {% elseif day > today and day <= 'now'|date_modify('+6 days')|date('Y-m-d') %}
                                        {{ insight.happensAt|intl_date('EEE') }}
                                    {% elseif insight.happensAt|date('Y') == 'now'|date('Y') %}
                                        {{ insight.happensAt|intl_date('dMMM') }}
                                    {% else %}
                                        {{ insight.happensAt|intl_date('dMMMy') }}
                                    {% endif %}

                                    {#- A parcel's ETA is a day, not an hour — its
                                        midnight is a placeholder, not a time. -#}
                                    {%- if insight.happensAt|date('His') != '000000' %} · {{ insight.happensAt|date(clock.time) }}{% endif %}
                                {% else %}
                                    {# A guard, not a feature. InsightPane hands
                                       this template only DATED rows — the radar
                                       panel is where the undated family lives, and
                                       a strip about what is coming up has nothing
                                       to say about a row with no when. The column
                                       is nullable all the same, and a blank line
                                       under a title reads as a render that failed,
                                       so the kind speaks instead. #}
                                    {{ insight.kind.transKey|trans }}
                                {% endif %}

                                {% if statusTone is not null %}
                                    <span data-insight-status="{{ status }}"
                                          class="ml-1 inline-flex items-center rounded-full border px-2 py-px
                                                 text-[11px] leading-[1.35] font-medium {{ statusTone }}">
                                        {{ ('insights.status.' ~ status)|trans }}
                                    </span>
                                {% endif %}
                            </p>
                        </div>

                        {# One primary action per row: the tracking page where there
                           is one, else the thing on GitHub. Never both — the strip's
                           whole claim is that it costs less attention than the mail
                           under it, and a row with two buttons has neither pressed. #}
                        {% if trackingUrl is not empty %}
                            <a href="{{ trackingUrl }}"
                               target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
                               data-insight-track
                               class="inline-flex shrink-0 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full bg-accent px-2.5 py-1
                                      text-xs font-medium text-accent-ink hover:bg-accent-strong transition-colors">
                                <i class="fa-solid fa-location-arrow text-[10px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                {{ 'insights.panel.track'|trans }}
                            </a>
                        {% elseif externalUrl is not empty %}
                            {# The brand's own name rather than a catalogue key —
                               "GitHub" is not a word any locale translates. #}
                            <a href="{{ externalUrl }}"
                               target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
                               data-insight-open-url
                               class="inline-flex shrink-0 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-line px-2.5 py-1
                                      text-xs font-medium text-ink-muted hover:bg-hover hover:text-ink transition-colors">
                                <i class="fa-brands fa-github text-[11px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                GitHub
                                <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-up-right-from-square text-[9px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                            </a>
                        {% endif %}

                        {# The row's own overflow menu. A second bare ✕ beside the
                           strip's would be two identical marks a pixel apart meaning
                           two different scopes — "this one" and "all of them" — which
                           is the press nobody can take back. Behind a `⋮` the item
                           can say which it is. #}
                        <div class="relative shrink-0" data-controller="ui--dropdown">
                            <button type="button"
                                    data-action="click->ui--dropdown#toggle"
                                    aria-label="{{ 'insights.pane.more'|trans }}"
                                    title="{{ 'insights.pane.more'|trans }}"
                                    class="flex h-7 w-7 items-center justify-center rounded-full
                                           text-ink-faint hover:bg-hover hover:text-ink transition-colors">
                                <i class="fa-solid fa-ellipsis-vertical text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                            </button>

                            <div data-ui--dropdown-target="menu" hidden
                                 class="absolute right-0 top-full mt-1 z-30 w-44
                                        rounded-pane bg-pane-soft backdrop-blur-sm
                                        border border-line shadow-pop py-1 text-sm">
                                <button type="button"
                                        data-action="click->insight--pane#dismiss click->ui--dropdown#close"
                                        data-insight--pane-url-param="{{ path('app_insight_dismiss', { id: insight.id }) }}"
                                        data-insight-dismiss
                                        class="flex w-full items-center gap-2 px-4 py-2 text-left text-ink-soft
                                               hover:bg-hover transition-colors">
                                    <i class="fa-solid fa-xmark w-4 text-ink-faint" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                    {{ 'insights.pane.dismiss'|trans }}
                                </button>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </li>
                {% endfor %}
            </ul>
        </div>
    {% endif %}
</turbo-frame>
